<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sino-Burmese War (1765–1769)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1765">1765</a>–<a href="/years/1769">1769</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Qing invasion of Burma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sino-Burmese War was fought from 1765 to 1769 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing China</a> and the Konbaung dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qianlong-emperor">Qianlong Emperor</a> sent four invasions into Burma, all of which were repulsed, the last ending with the Treaty of Kaungton (1769); Burma kept its independence, but the war diverted it from its campaigns against Siam.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sino-burmese-war-1765-1769.jpg" alt="Sino-Burmese War (1765–1769)" width="320" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: w:User:Soewinhan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Qing_and_Konbaung_before_Sino_Burmese_War.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
